
{% macro head(kick, title, n) -%}
<div class="kicker">{{kick}}</div><div class="hrule"></div><img class="qmark" src="{{qmark}}">
<div class="title">{{title}}</div><div class="sub">{{S.name}}&nbsp; / &nbsp;{{S.rec.locality}}</div>
<div class="foot"><b>{{'%02d' % n}}</b><span>{{S.report_id}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{DATE}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{REV}}</span></div>
{%- endmacro %}

<!-- 01 COVER -->
<section class="page">
  <img src="{{logo}}" style="position:absolute;left:18mm;top:20mm;width:69mm">
  <div style="position:absolute;right:18.5mm;top:57mm;text-align:right;font-style:italic;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.45">Better study,<br>better decisions.</div>
  <img src="{{layers_cover}}" style="position:absolute;left:135.7mm;top:77.5mm;width:74.3mm">
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17mm;top:80mm;font-size:52pt;font-weight:700;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-1pt">Kogilu<br>Site<br>Report</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:149mm;font-size:12.5pt;color:#333">Site 3 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Sy. 27 &amp; 28 &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{fmt(geo.area_acre,2)}} acres</div>
  <div class="glbl" style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:201mm;font-size:7pt">Site analysis</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:211mm;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.5">Prepared for Qnit case-study portfolio<br>Presented by GeoAce Studio Pvt Ltd</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:233.5mm;font-size:8pt;color:#666;line-height:1.55">Kogilu, Yelahanka, Bengaluru North &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{geo.centroid[0]}}° N, {{geo.centroid[1]}}° E<br>{{DATE}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{REV}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{S.report_id}}</div>
  <img src="{{geoace}}" style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:264mm;width:47mm">
</section>

<!-- 02 OVERVIEW -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SITE OVERVIEW','The site at a glance',2) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:5.6mm">
   <div style="width:135.5mm"><img class="fig" src="{{fig.hero}}" style="height:81mm"></div>
   <div class="col" style="padding-top:.6mm">
     <div class="lbl">Latitude</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:13pt">{{'%.6f' % geo.centroid[0]}}° N</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Longitude</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:13pt">{{'%.6f' % geo.centroid[1]}}° E</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Study extent</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:16pt">{{fmt(geo.study_extent_m)}} m</div>
     <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm">North up · scale bar on image<br>Imagery Wayback 24 Sep 2026</div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Esri World Imagery (Wayback 2026-09-24). Boundary from Case_Studies.kml, Site 3; vertices V1–V4, centroid in WGS 84.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:9mm;gap:0">
   <div style="width:72mm"><div class="lbl">Site area</div><div class="big">{{fmt(geo.area_m2)}} m²</div><div class="small">{{fmt(geo.area_acre,2)}} acres · {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha · {{fmt(geo.area_guntas)}} guntas</div></div>
   <div style="width:56mm"><div class="lbl">Perimeter</div><div class="big">{{fmt(geo.perimeter_m)}} m</div><div class="small">KML boundary, Oct 2026</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Boundary</div><div class="big">{{geo.n_edges}} edges</div><div class="small">Quadrilateral, about {{geo.rect_dims_m[0]}} × {{geo.rect_dims_m[1]}} m</div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:8mm">Design brief</h2>
  <p style="font-size:11.6pt;line-height:1.33">A {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha residential parcel in Kogilu, north Bengaluru, already subdivided as a plotted layout. What can it carry under RMP 2015 Residential (Main) controls, and which edge, buffer and height clearance sets the limit?</p>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6mm">
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Primary opportunity</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.8pt">{{zone_top[1]}}% of the parcel reads Residential on the draft RMP 2031 layer; Residential (Main) on approved RMP 2015. A school is a {{poi.Education[0].walk_min|int}}-min walk and Yelahanka metro (Blue Line 2B) is due 2027–28: group housing at FAR 2.25–2.50 is the natural programme.</p></div>
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Key constraint</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.8pt">A mapped stream runs {{fmt(streams_d)}} m off the west edge (D–A) in the valley "sensitive area". A 25–50 m drain buffer takes {{fmt(buf[25])}}–{{fmt(buf[50])}} m² ({{'%.1f'|format(100*buf[25]/geo.area_m2)}}–{{'%.1f'|format(100*buf[50]/geo.area_m2)}}%). Buildings of 15 m or more need Yelahanka AFS clearance.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #d4d4d4;margin-top:6mm;padding-top:4.2mm;display:flex">
   <div class="glbl" style="width:56mm;font-size:7.4pt;padding-top:1mm">Report route</div>
   <div class="small" style="font-size:7.6pt">03–04 &nbsp;Site &amp; ground &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 05–08 &nbsp;Environment<br>09–11 &nbsp;Context &amp; services &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 12 &nbsp;Priorities &amp; sources</div>
  </div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:4.5mm">Stakeholders: Qnit case-study portfolio &nbsp;/&nbsp; GeoAce Studio design team &nbsp;/&nbsp; Reviewer: pending</div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SITE DETAILS -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SITE DETAILS','Boundary, edges & development',3) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:3mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.boundary}}" style="width:101mm;height:75mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.zoning_screenshot}}" style="width:71mm;height:75mm;object-position:28% 50%">
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Left: Esri imagery 2026; stream from Overture Maps (2026-09); dashed = draft RMP 2031 plan roads (Qnit planning layer). Right: Qnit 2031 plan layer, BDA RMP 2031 (draft), supplied screenshot.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6.5mm;gap:13mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Site identity</h2><div class="kv">
     <div>Survey / parcel &nbsp;<b>Sy. 27/*/1 · 28/*/XX</b></div>
     <div>Village / authority &nbsp;<b>Kogilu (938519) · BDA</b></div>
     <div>CRS / boundary &nbsp;<b>WGS 84 KML · UTM 43N</b></div>
     <div>Records / status &nbsp;<b>RCCMS: no cases · no mutations</b></div></div></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>Development controls</h2><div class="kv">
     <div>Permitted use / source &nbsp;<b>Residential (Main) · RMP 2015</b></div>
     <div>FAR / coverage &nbsp;<b>2.25–2.50 / 55% (18 m road)</b></div>
     <div>Setbacks F / R / sides &nbsp;<b>≥ 5 m all round; 5–16 m by height</b></div>
     <div>Height limit / basis &nbsp;<b>&lt; 15 m without AFS NOC</b></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:5.5mm;border:0;padding:0;margin-bottom:3mm">Edge conditions</h2>
  <table class="t">
   <tr><th style="width:15mm">Edge</th><th>Adjoining condition</th><th style="width:44mm">Clearance / width</th><th style="width:38mm">Evidence</th></tr>
   <tr><td>A–B · S</td><td>Tree belt (plantation strip), open land; {{lake1.name}} beyond</td><td>{{lake1.name}} {{fmt(lake1.dist_m)}} m S; plan 18 m road {{fmt(proad.dist_m)}} m SE</td><td>Esri 2026 · Overture · RMP 2031 layer</td></tr>
   <tr><td>B–C · E</td><td>Local residential road; open plots and low sheds</td><td>Road width not mapped; survey needed</td><td>Overture 2026-09 · Esri 2026</td></tr>
   <tr><td>C–D · N</td><td>Vacant plot with earth track; 1–2 storey houses beyond</td><td>No frontage road</td><td>Esri 2026 · Overture buildings</td></tr>
   <tr><td>D–A · W</td><td>Earth track, mapped stream in the valley strip; brick and sand yards beyond</td><td>Stream {{fmt(streams_d)}} m; primary drain {{fmt(drain1)}} m SW</td><td>Overture water · BBMP SWD 2022</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>The west edge controls. RMP 2015 sets 15 / 25 / 50 m drain buffers by drain class: here that is {{fmt(buf[15])}} / {{fmt(buf[25])}} / {{fmt(buf[50])}} m² of the site. Confirm the drain class with GBA (SWD) and the revenue sketch, and the widths of the E and W roads, before fixing the layout.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 TOPOGRAPHY -->
<section class="page">{{ head('TOPOGRAPHY','Terrain & the ground beneath',4) }}
 <div class="body">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.terrain}}" style="height:96mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Copernicus GLO-30 DSM (30 m, resampled to 10 m), 1 m contours, over Esri imagery. A–B follows the fitted fall line.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7.5mm;gap:0">
   <div style="width:72mm"><div class="lbl">Elevation range</div><div class="big">{{'%.0f'|format(ter.elev_min)}} / {{'%.0f'|format(ter.elev_max)}} m</div><div class="small">EGM2008 · DSM includes canopy</div></div>
   <div style="width:56mm"><div class="lbl">Typical slope</div><div class="big">{{'%.1f'|format(ter.plane_slope_pct)}} %</div><div class="small">Gentle · falls to the {{ter.fall_dir}}</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Contour interval</div><div class="big">{{ter.contour_interval_m}} m</div><div class="small">GLO-30 DSM / 30 m</div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:7.5mm">Transect A–B</h2>
  <img src="{{fig.transect}}" style="width:100%;height:29mm;object-fit:contain">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Section A–B sampled every 5 m from the DSM; A is south-east, B north-west.</div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:3.5mm;font-size:8pt">Section length {{fmt(tr.length_m)}} m &nbsp; / &nbsp; Relief {{'%.1f'|format(tr.relief_m)}} m &nbsp; / &nbsp; Vertical exaggeration ≈ {{'%.0f'|format(ve)}}×</div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>About {{'%.0f'|format(ter.relief_m)}} m of fall across the parcel, {{'%.1f'|format(ter.plane_slope_pct)}}% to the {{ter.fall_dir}}; the low point ({{'%.0f'|format(ter.low_pt_z)}} m) is the north-west corner, where runoff leaves for the western valley. Step block platforms by 0.5–1 m; no tall retaining walls are indicated. Confirm with a ground survey, as the DSM includes trees.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 SUN -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SUN & SOLAR EXPOSURE','Light, shade & orientation',5) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <div style="width:110mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">01 &nbsp;/&nbsp; Sun path</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.sunpath}}" style="height:87mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">Seasonal comparison</div><img src="{{fig.sunpolar}}" style="width:100%;height:57mm;object-fit:contain">
     <div class="small" style="margin-top:3mm">21 Mar · 21 Jun · 21 Dec; {{sol.tz}}<br>True north; noon altitude {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].noon_alt)}}° (Dec) to {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Jun'].noon_alt)}}° (Jun, sun to the north)<br>Day length {{'%.1f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].daylength_h)}}–{{'%.1f'|format(sol.events['21 Jun'].daylength_h)}} h; no context model</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Solar positions computed (NREL SPA, pvlib) for the site centroid; stereographic dome, Esri imagery. Hour lines at the 21st of each month.</div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #ddd;margin-top:5.5mm;padding-top:5mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">02 &nbsp;/&nbsp; Solar radiation</div>
  <div class="row" style="gap:7mm">
   <div style="width:92mm"><img src="{{fig.solar}}" style="width:100%;height:65mm;object-fit:contain"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Analysis period</div><div class="mid">{{sol.years[0]}}–{{sol.years[1]}} monthly means</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Incident solar energy</div><div class="big" style="font-size:23pt">{{fmt(sol.ghi_year_kwh)}} kWh/m²</div>
     <div class="small">Horizontal plane, per year ({{'%.2f'|format(sol.ghi_day_mean)}} kWh/m²·day)<br>Highest wall exposure: SE / SW ≈ {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.SE)}}; north {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.N)}}<br>Best month {{MON[sol.best_month-1]}}; cloud cuts {{sol.cloud_loss_pct|int}}% vs clear sky</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NASA POWER CERES SYN1deg monthly GHI {{sol.years[0]}}–{{sol.years[1]}}; wall split modelled from clear-sky geometry scaled to it.</div></div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>The long axis runs E–W ({{geo.long_axis_deg|int}}°), so blocks can face north and south: the noon sun stays above {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].noon_alt)}}°, and short overhangs shade both faces. East and west walls take ≈ {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.E)}} kWh/m²·yr: limit glazing there. Roofs suit PV.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 06 WIND -->
<section class="page">{{ head('WIND & MICROCLIMATE','Air movement & outdoor comfort',6) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.windmap}}" style="width:121mm;height:81mm">
   <div class="col"><img src="{{fig.windrose}}" style="width:100%;height:50mm;object-fit:contain">
    <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:4mm">Season / height</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:11.5pt">2015–24 / 10 m</div>
    <div class="small">Annual: from {{wst.annual.prevailing}}, mean {{wst.annual.mean_speed}} m/s, calm {{wst.annual.calm_pct}}%<br>Jun–Sep: {{sm.prevailing}} {{sm.prevailing_pct|int}}%, {{sm.mean_speed}} m/s<br>Dec–Feb: {{wi.prevailing}} {{wi.prevailing_pct|int}}%, {{wi.mean_speed}} m/s</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NOAA ISD hourly observations, Kempegowda Intl Airport (VOBL), {{af['KIA (VOBL) ARP'].dist_km}} km NE; agrees with NASA POWER MERRA-2 (from {{wmd.annual.prevailing}}, {{wmd.annual.mean_speed}} m/s).</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Local comfort</h2><img class="fig" src="{{fig.comfort}}" style="height:62mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>Seasonal temperature</h2><img src="{{fig.temperature}}" style="width:100%;height:62mm;object-fit:contain"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="row"><div class="col cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; ESA WorldCover 2021 (10 m) on Esri imagery; dashed = 500 m ring.</div>
  <div class="col cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NASA POWER MERRA-2 daily, {{cli.years[0]}}–{{cli.years[1]}}. VOBL station mean {{wst.t_mean}} °C vs model {{cli.t_annual_mean}} °C.</div></div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Run internal streets and gaps E–W so the June–September westerly ({{sm.mean_speed}} m/s) flushes the layout, entering over the open west valley. April is the hot month (mean max {{cli.tmax_peak[0]}} °C): keep the southern tree belt and shade play areas and parking.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 07 RAIN -->
<section class="page">{{ head('RAINFALL & WATER','Runoff, storage & groundwater',7) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <div style="width:110mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">Surface response</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.runoff}}" style="height:79mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:2mm">Monthly rainfall</div><img src="{{fig.rainfall}}" style="width:100%;height:31mm;object-fit:contain">
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:7mm">Event basis</div><div class="big" style="font-size:20pt">{{q10|int}} mm / 24 h</div>
     <div class="small">10-year return period (Gumbel on {{cli.amax_1day_years[0]}}–{{cli.amax_1day_years[1]}} annual maxima)<br>Mean annual {{fmt(cli.rain_annual_mean)}} mm; {{cli.rain_jun_nov_pct|int}}% falls May–Nov</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; D8 flow on GLO-30 DSM; Overture water; BBMP primary storm drains (SWD 2022). Rain: NASA POWER MERRA-2 grid {{cli.grid[0]}} N {{cli.grid[1]}} E.</div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:6mm">Groundwater &amp; recharge</h2>
  <img src="{{fig.groundwater}}" style="width:100%;height:27mm;object-fit:contain">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Conceptual section on A–B. Strata and water depths from the CGWB Bengaluru Urban profile, not site boreholes.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6mm">
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Surface water</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">Low point NW corner ({{'%.0f'|format(ter.low_pt_z)}} m) → west stream → primary drain {{fmt(drain1)}} m SW → {{lake1.name}}.<br>10-yr day on {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha: ≈ {{fmt(vol_now,-2)}} m³ runoff now (C 0.35), ≈ {{fmt(vol_built,-2)}} m³ built (C 0.75).<br>Basis: catchment = site; land cover WorldCover 2021.</p></div>
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Ground conditions</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">District water level 5–30 m bgl pre-monsoon (CGWB).<br>Bengaluru North extraction over 200% of recharge (2024): over-exploited.<br>Weathered gneiss 10–30 m over fractured rock; percolation to be tested.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Keep the NW corner and west edge as the drainage and detention zone, sized for ≈ {{fmt(vol_built - vol_now,-2)}} m³ of extra runoff once built; do not culvert the stream. Plan water on Cauvery Stage V or treated reuse, not new borewells.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 08 LANDSCAPE -->
<section class="page">{{ head('LANDSCAPE & ECOLOGY','Living systems & views',8) }}
 <div class="body">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.landscape}}" style="height:92mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Esri imagery; Overture water bodies; plan-view sight lines from the site centre to the three nearest named lakes.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7mm;gap:13mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Landscape structure</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:3mm;margin:3mm 0 1mm"><img src="{{ic_land}}" style="width:29%"><img src="{{ic_veg}}" style="width:29%"><img src="{{ic_built}}" style="width:29%"></div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:3mm" class="small"><div style="width:32%">Landform</div><div style="width:32%">Vegetation</div><div style="width:32%">Built form</div></div>
    <div class="kv" style="margin-top:5mm">
     <div>Canopy cover &nbsp;<b>{{'%.0f'|format(lc.canopy_site)}}% site · {{'%.0f'|format(lc.canopy_ring)}}% 500 m ring</b></div>
     <div>Permeable ground &nbsp;<b>{{'%.0f'|format(lc.permeable_site)}}% (2021) · {{'%.0f'|format(lc.permeable_ring)}}% ring</b></div>
     <div>Water / habitat edge &nbsp;<b>stream {{fmt(streams_d)}} m · {{lake1.name}} {{fmt(lake1.dist_m)}} m</b></div>
     <div>Tree survey / season &nbsp;<b>none · WorldCover 2021</b></div></div></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>View &amp; habitat priorities</h2>
    <div class="txt" style="font-size:9pt;line-height:1.45">Retain<br><b style="font-weight:400">The southern tree belt along A–B and the west valley corridor linking to {{lake1.name}}.</b><br><br>Investigate<br><b style="font-weight:400">Lake views are screened at ground level; upper floors gain them, but heights of 15 m or more need AFS clearance.</b></div>
    <div class="small" style="margin-top:9mm">Observer: site centre, plan view (no eye-height model)<br>Vegetation 2021 predates the layout roads; built cover now higher</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Put the statutory 10% park ({{fmt(park10)}} m², RMP 2015 large-plot rule) along the west valley, so it doubles as the drain buffer and the green link to {{lake1.name}}.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 09 CONTEXT -->
<section class="page">{{ head('BUILT CONTEXT & ACCESS','Neighbourhood fit & movement',9) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.context}}" style="height:71mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Overture Maps buildings and roads (release 2026-09-23) over Esri imagery; A–B is a 1.2 km W–E section through the site.</div>
  <div class="glbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Street &amp; skyline profile A–B</div>
  <img src="{{fig.skyline}}" style="width:100%;height:21mm;object-fit:contain;margin-top:2mm">
  <div class="cap" style="margin-top:1mm">{{sky.n}} buildings cut; none carry mapped heights, so hatched blocks use storeys assumed from footprint (2–4 floors × 3.2 m).</div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #ddd;margin-top:4mm;padding-top:4mm" class="row">
   <div style="width:76mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3mm">Daily access</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.isochrones}}" style="height:70mm">
    <div class="cap">Walking 5 / 10 / 15 min at 4.8 km/h on the Overture road network from the layout roads.</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Access basis</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:12pt">Layout roads / walk / weekday</div>
    <div class="kv" style="margin-top:4mm">
     <div>Transit &nbsp;<b>{{inf.bus_stop.name}} stop · {{fmt(inf.bus_stop.dist_m)}} m</b></div>
     <div>Rail &nbsp;<b>Yelahanka Jn · {{'%.1f'|format(inf.railway_station.dist_m/1000)}} km; metro due 2027–28</b></div>
     <div>Health &nbsp;<b>{{poi.Health[0].name}} · {{poi.Health[0].walk_min|int}} min</b></div>
     <div>Education &nbsp;<b>{{poi.Education[0].name}} · {{poi.Education[0].walk_min|int}} min</b></div>
     <div>Daily needs &nbsp;<b>{{grocery.name}} · {{grocery.walk_min|int}} min</b></div></div>
    <div class="txt" style="margin-top:5mm;font-weight:700;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.4">No mapped road on the N and S edges; access relies on the E and W lanes. NH-44 (Bellary Rd) is {{'%.1f'|format(R.context.major_roads.trunk.dist_m/1000)}} km W.<br>Context is 1–3 storey houses (median footprint {{R.context.bld_500_footprint_median|int}} m²) with {{R.context.bld_500_large_n}} large blocks: mid-rise up to 15 m fits.</div>
    <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm">Overture 2026-09-23.0 · checked {{DATE}}</div></div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

