  </div>
  <div style="font-size:14.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin-top:6.5mm">Raised, shaded thresholds — jagali and veranda — mediate between the street and the home, and suit Kogilu's hot April and westerly monsoon wind.</div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm;font-size:6.9pt">Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0: Prof tpms (Melukote, Krishnarajapet, Malavalli); Bharathesha Alasandemajalu (Puttur) &nbsp;/&nbsp; Old Mysore and coastal Karnataka examples, not on-site records</div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Give each block a raised, shaded front threshold onto the internal street: a contemporary jagali that also keeps entrances above the monsoon runoff.</p></div>
